    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Testing the validate method with alternative date/time values:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "validate at now + 10 mins - success",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "validate at now - 10 mins - fail - expected",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "So this would fix the test case.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I note that in the REST API tests at least, there is very little explicit testing of asOfDateTime parameter to check it gets the right version (especially at a degree of precision; we should be testing 1ms before, now, 1ms after on a few methods to check this behaviour).",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "So in conclusion, no idea why this was specifically failing on Postgresql, I can only suggest that the alternative database caused some variation in execution time of various methods in the test class, and that triggered the error.  But I don't think that this failure was revealing an underlying bug.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
