      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8e627ad1f07d2a95bfd257d6c78c26a6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-6.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8e627ad1f07d2a95bfd257d6c78c26a6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8e627ad1f07d2a95bfd257d6c78c26a6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8e627ad1f07d2a95bfd257d6c78c26a6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Aaron Birkland",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Apppears to always occur when there is an asOfDateTime specified:  <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/fedora/objects/demo:REST/validate?asOfDateTime=2011-05-21T15:54:50.215Z\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/fedora/objects/demo:REST/validate?asOfDateTime=2011-05-21T15:54:50.215Z</a>.  Need to find out why the choice of database makes a difference, though.</p>",
     "created": "21/May/11 6:07 PM",
     "id": "11964",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10938/comment/11964",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8e627ad1f07d2a95bfd257d6c78c26a6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-6.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8e627ad1f07d2a95bfd257d6c78c26a6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8e627ad1f07d2a95bfd257d6c78c26a6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8e627ad1f07d2a95bfd257d6c78c26a6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Aaron Birkland",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "21/May/11 6:07 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I've reproduced this.</p>\n\n<p>The failure is on demo:REST - and this object has its date/time settings set to the current date/time - and the asOfDateTime is set to exactly the same value.</p>\n\n<p>So I wonder if this is something to do with date comparison/precision that is specific to postgresql</p>\n\n<p>The validation is failing because of a missing DC datastream, which is of course impossible - so I'd suggest that it is not actually picking the datastream up because of something awry in the date/time querying/comparison.</p>\n",
     "created": "23/May/11 12:57 PM",
     "id": "11965",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10938/comment/11965",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "23/May/11 12:57 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Further observations</p>\n\n<p>String datetime is set to current date (new Date()) as a static at class level</p>\n\n<p>test object demo:REST has CREATED set for datastreams RELS-EXT and RELS-INT, but <b>not</b> for DC to this value</p>\n\n<p>Ingest will take place (theoretically?) <b>after</b> datetime - so DC will have a created date later than datetime (as will the object creation date/time)</p>\n\n<p>So the validate is failing correctly - it is validating the object at an earlier datetime than the created date for DC - so DC won't have any versions present.</p>\n\n<p>The behaviour now seems correct to me - but I have no idea why this should have not been failing on other databases - perhaps with Derby the whole thing is running faster and the ingest date/time is in fact (to the date/time precision) the same as datetime set at class level?  I would have expected the odd spurious test failure from time-to-time.</p>",
     "created": "25/May/11 8:21 AM",
     "id": "11969",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10938/comment/11969",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "25/May/11 8:25 AM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Testing the validate method with alternative date/time values:</p>\n\n<p>validate at now + 10 mins - success<br/>\nvalidate at now - 10 mins - fail - expected</p>\n\n<p>So this would fix the test case.</p>\n\n<p>I note that in the REST API tests at least, there is very little explicit testing of asOfDateTime parameter to check it gets the right version (especially at a degree of precision; we should be testing 1ms before, now, 1ms after on a few methods to check this behaviour).</p>\n\n<p>So in conclusion, no idea why this was specifically failing on Postgresql, I can only suggest that the alternative database caused some variation in execution time of various methods in the test class, and that triggered the error.  But I don't think that this failure was revealing an underlying bug.</p>",
     "created": "25/May/11 8:50 AM",
     "id": "11970",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10938/comment/11970",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
